<%- include('partials/mkt_header', {
  title: "Privacy Policy — Uma's Books",
  description: "How Uma's Books collects, uses, shares and keeps your personal data, for how long, and how to exercise your rights.",
}) %>
  <div class="page-hero">
    <span class="kicker" data-i18n="pp.kicker">Legal</span>
    <h1 data-i18n="pp.title">Privacy Policy</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="muted small" data-i18n="pp.updated">Last updated: October 2026.</p>

      <p data-i18n-html="pp.intro">This page explains, in plain language, what personal data we collect through this website, why, who receives it, how long we keep it, and how you can access or delete it. Questions? Write to <a href="mailto:admin@umasbooks.org">admin@umasbooks.org</a>.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s1.h">Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p data-i18n-html="pp.s1.p"><strong>Uma’s Books</strong>, a non-profit association under the French law of 1 July 1901 (RNA W811011706, SIRET 109 441 147 00013), whose registered office is at 5, rue Hippolyte Savary, 81000 Albi, France, is the data controller. It is represented by its President. We are a volunteer-run, non-profit secondhand English-language bookshop and community space in Albi. See also our <a href="mentions-legales.html">legal notice</a>.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s2.h">What we collect, why, and on what basis</h2>
      <p data-i18n="pp.s2.p1">We only collect what we need to run the shop, our programs and our community, and almost all of it comes directly from you:</p>
      <ul data-i18n-html="pp.s2.list">
        <li><strong>Account:</strong> email, name, a password (stored only as a one-way scrambled hash, never in plain text), the date of your last login and the number of failed login attempts. <em>Why:</em> to let you log in, place orders, become a member, keep favorites and use member features, and to protect accounts from guessing. <em>Basis:</em> performance of the service you asked for; our legitimate interest in security.</li>
        <li><strong>Orders and reservations:</strong> name, email, phone number, and what you bought or reserved. Orders are placed with an account: your order is linked to your account and uses its confirmed email address. <em>Why:</em> to fulfil your order, hold a book for pickup and send you confirmations and reminders. <em>Basis:</em> contract; legal obligation (accounting).</li>
        <li><strong>Payments and membership:</strong> online payments are handled entirely by our payment provider HelloAsso; we never see or store your card details. We receive the payer’s email, the amount and the date, to match a membership payment to your account. <em>Basis:</em> contract; legal obligation (accounting).</li>
        <li><strong>Event and session sign-ups:</strong> name and email. <em>Why:</em> to manage attendance and capacity. <em>Basis:</em> contract.</li><li><strong>Book requests:</strong> the title (and author or ISBN) of the book you ask for, your email, and optionally your name and a note. <em>Why:</em> to confirm your request, and to email you if we find the book. <em>Basis:</em> your request.</li>
        <li><strong>Messages you send us</strong> (contact form, volunteer sign-up and English Immersion pre-registration): name, email, phone and what you write. For a pre-registration, also the child’s name and date of birth, the days and times that suit you and the details you add; these come from the child’s parent or legal guardian. These forms send us an email and nothing is stored on the website itself. Please do not enter health information in them: tell us in person. <em>Why:</em> to reply and organise activities. <em>Basis:</em> your request; our legitimate interest in answering.</li>
        <li><strong>Community content:</strong> forum posts, charity votes and ideas, volunteer shifts and meeting RSVPs. Posts are visible to other members. <em>Basis:</em> contract and, for posts, your choice to publish.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> your IP address and browser details are processed briefly to keep the site running and to limit abuse, and appear in the server logs of our hosting provider and of Cloudflare, the network in front of the site. The IP address kept with an order, to limit abuse of the checkout, is deleted after 2 days. <em>Basis:</em> legitimate interest in security.</li>
      </ul>
      <p data-i18n="pp.s2.p2">When you choose a password we also check it against a public list of breached passwords, in a way that never reveals your password or your email to that service. We do not use your data for advertising, profiling or automated decisions, and we never sell it.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.photos.h">Photos and videos</h2>
      <p data-i18n="pp.photos.p">We never take photographs or videos of customers, members or children without their consent. For a child, we first ask for the consent of a parent or legal guardian. You can withdraw your consent at any time by writing to us (see Contact), and we will then stop using the image.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s3.h">Cookies, local storage and fonts</h2>
      <p data-i18n="pp.s3.p">We use one session cookie (umasbooks.sid) to keep you logged in and remember your cart; it lasts up to 30 days. We also set a language cookie (umasbooks_lang) for one year: it stores only EN or FR, so that the pages we send you are in your language. Both are strictly necessary for the site to work and to remember your choice, so no consent banner is required. Your browser’s local storage holds the same language choice (umasbooks.lang) and, if you are not logged in, the books you favorited on that device (umasbooks.favorites); it stays on your device. We use no advertising, tracking or audience-measurement cookies. The HelloAsso payment form on the membership page is not loaded until you click “Show the HelloAsso form”; once it is, HelloAsso receives your IP address and may set its own cookies needed for payment. Book covers are shown from our own server, so your browser contacts no other company to get them.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s4.h">Who receives your data</h2>
      <p data-i18n="pp.s4.p1">We never sell or rent your data. It is shared only with the services that help us run the site, each receiving only what it needs:</p>
      <ul data-i18n-html="pp.s4.list">
        <li><strong>HelloAsso</strong> (France) — online payments and memberships; it also acts as an independent controller for the payment data you give it.</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong> (Google Workspace / Gmail) — our email, used to send confirmations and to receive your messages.</li>
        <li><strong>Render</strong> — hosts the website and its database, in its European (Frankfurt, Germany) region.</li><li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (United States) — the content-delivery and security network that Render places in front of the website. Every request passes through it, so it sees visitors’ IP addresses and relays the traffic (including what you type in forms) to our host; we use it for nothing else.</li>
        <li><strong>Backblaze</strong> — stores private backups of our database in its European data centre so we can recover from a failure.</li>
        <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> (United States) — an AI service our administrators use to look up book information (awards, descriptions, genres and used-book prices) and to read book cover photos. It receives only book details such as title, author and ISBN, or a photo of a book cover: never personal data about customers or members.</li>
      </ul>
      <p data-i18n="pp.s4.p2">Some of these providers are US companies. Where your data is handled outside the European Union, it is under the safeguards the GDPR requires, such as standard contractual clauses or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. We may also disclose data when the law requires it. When our administrators look up book details and download cover images from Open Library and the Internet Archive, the requests come from our server and contain only book details (title, author, ISBN): no visitor’s data or address is sent to them, and your browser never loads images from them.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s5.h">How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul data-i18n-html="pp.s5.list">
        <li><strong>Accounts whose email was never confirmed:</strong> deleted after 7 days.</li><li><strong>Member account:</strong> until you ask us to delete it, or after 3 years without logging in (we email you 30 days before deleting it, and logging in keeps it).</li>
        <li><strong>Orders and payment records:</strong> 10 years, as French accounting law requires; after that they are deleted. Contact details on old orders are removed earlier if you ask and the law allows.</li>
        <li><strong>Reservation details:</strong> deleted automatically when the 14-day hold ends, or 30 days after a reservation is sold or cancelled. Contact details on orders that were never completed (expired or cancelled) are removed after 30 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Event and session sign-ups:</strong> 12 months after the event.</li><li><strong>Book requests:</strong> until you cancel, or 12 months at most; deleted within 30 days after we find the book.</li>
        <li><strong>Messages you send us:</strong> emails received through the contact, volunteer sign-up and pre-registration forms are kept 12 months in our mailbox, then deleted, unless a conversation is still ongoing.</li>
        <li><strong>Forum posts, charity ideas and votes:</strong> while your account exists; when you delete your account, the forum posts and charity ideas you wrote stay but without your name.</li>
        <li><strong>Backups:</strong> nightly copies for 30 days, monthly copies for up to 2 years. A deletion therefore disappears from backups within that time.</li>
        <li><strong>IP address kept with an order</strong> (to limit abuse of the checkout): 2 days.</li><li><strong>Cookies:</strong> session cookie up to 30 days, language cookie 1 year.</li><li><strong>Server logs:</strong> a few weeks at most.</li>
        <li><strong>Administrator action log:</strong> 12 months; the free-text note of an entry (for example a refund reason) is erased after 6 months.</li><li><strong>Copies of the emails we send you</strong> (confirmations, links, reminders; kept so we can resend an email that did not arrive): 30 days after sending, 90 days for an email that could not be sent; then the address, subject and text are erased.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s6.h">Your rights</h2>
      <p data-i18n-html="pp.s6.p1">Under the GDPR and French data protection law you can ask us to <strong>access</strong> your data, <strong>correct</strong> it, <strong>delete</strong> it, <strong>restrict</strong> its use, give it to you in a portable format, or <strong>object</strong> to how we use it, and you can withdraw any consent you gave at any time. To exercise a right, write to us at <a href="mailto:admin@umasbooks.org">admin@umasbooks.org</a>; we may ask you to prove you own the address (for example by replying from it), and we will answer within <strong>one month</strong>. You can also download or delete your own data yourself from <a href="/account/privacy">My Account &gt; Privacy</a>.</p>
      <p data-i18n="pp.s6.p2">If you believe we have not handled your data properly, you may complain to France’s data protection authority, the CNIL: CNIL, 3 Place de Fontenoy, TSA 80715, 75334 Paris Cedex 07 — cnil.fr.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s7.h">Children</h2>
      <p data-i18n="pp.s7.p">Our English Immersion program is for children as well as adults. When a parent or guardian registers a child, they provide that information with their responsibility and consent. We collect only what is needed to run the activity, and we do not create accounts for children. On the pre-registration form the parent or legal guardian confirms that they are the child’s parent or guardian and agrees to be contacted, and is asked not to enter any health information. A child’s details are kept 12 months in our mailbox, then deleted.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s8.h">Security</h2>
      <p data-i18n="pp.s8.p">We take reasonable measures to protect your data: passwords are never stored in plain text, connections to this site are encrypted (HTTPS), access to administration is restricted, and we keep tested backups. No online service can guarantee absolute security. If a breach were likely to put you at risk, we would tell you and the CNIL as the law requires.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s9.h">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p data-i18n="pp.s9.p">If we make significant changes to this policy, we will update the date at the top of this page.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="pp.s10.h">Contact</h2>
      <p data-i18n-html="pp.s10.p">Questions about this policy or your data: <a href="mailto:admin@umasbooks.org">admin@umasbooks.org</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
